# Open record is NOT a subtype of a closed record (negative direction)
# Companion to open_record_accepts_closed.llt-eval (which tests the positive direction).
#
# f accepts a CLOSED record [x: Int] — no extra fields allowed.
# g's parameter r has open-record type [x: Int ...] from its annotation.
# Passing $r to $f inside g must fail: is_subtype(open, closed) = false (Rémy 1994).
#
# The eval/typecheck corpus runner (test_typecheck_corpus) is currently disabled
# (requires typecheck-stdlib-types sprint). The type-error scenario is exercised by
# test_open_record_not_subtype_of_closed in src/typecheck.rs.
[f: [fn [r@[type: [x: Int]]] $r]
 g: [fn [r@[type: [x: Int ...]]] [call $f $r]]]
===
TYPE_ERROR: type mismatch
